{"seq":35,"t":745.608,"campaign_id":"li-conductor","body":{"type":"analyst.verdict","hypothesis_id":"h1","verdict":"REFUTED","reasoning":"The predicted correlation is absent, so the hypothesis fails on its own stated criterion. Stability and mobility are separate axes here, which means the search cannot be collapsed \u2014 it has to stay multi-objective. Spearman rho = -1.00 across 4 candidates (prediction required > 0.50). The most stable candidate (0.000 eV/atom above hull) has a barrier of 0.59 eV, while the lowest barrier measured is 0.14 eV at 0.007 eV/atom above hull.","evidence":["Spearman rho = -1.00 across 4 candidates (prediction required > 0.50). The most stable candidate (0.000 eV/atom above hull) has a barrier of 0.59 eV, while the lowest barrier measured is 0.14 eV at 0.007 eV/atom above hull."],"heuristics":[{"id":"heu-1","text":"Do not screen Li conductors on stability alone \u2014 in the thiophosphates, proximity to the hull does not predict the migration barrier. Score both axes.","learned_from":"h1","strength":"tentative"},{"id":"heu-2","text":"Straight-line hop energies are upper bounds and carry an OOD flag. Treat differences smaller than ~0.1 eV between candidates as noise.","learned_from":"h1","strength":"established"}]}}
